From: Curd Becker <me@curd-becker.de>
Subject: [PATCH] regulator: tps65910: optionally keep external sleep control at shutdown

tps65910_shutdown() takes every regulator off its external sleep control
(EN1, EN2, SLEEP) so that a bootloader finds the rails driven by their
registers after a reset.

On the Microsoft Surface RT the firmware hands the CPU rail (TPS65911
VDDCTRL) over assigned to EN1, with VDDCtrl_SR = 0, and clearing
VDDCTRL_EN1 drops the rail at once. The board then hangs in the driver
shutdown phase, before the PMIC power-off or restart command is sent:
reboot and poweroff leave the device dark with the PMIC still on, until a
long press of the power button. The firmware's own ResetSystem clears
VDDCTRL_EN1 as well, but as its last step right before the SoC reset.

Add the boolean property ti,keep-ext-sleep-control-on-shutdown, which
leaves the external control as it is at shutdown; the PMIC's power-off and
restart (DEV_OFF, DEV_OFF_RST) end it along with everything else. Set it
for the Tegra30 Windows RT devices: Surface RT, ASUS VivoTab RT (TF600T)
and Lenovo IdeaPad Yoga 11. They run the same NVIDIA Windows platform
drivers and carry the same EN1 control of vdd_cpu in their device trees.

Tested on the Surface RT: reboot and poweroff work. The TF600T and the
Yoga 11 are untested; testers welcome.
---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/ti,tps65910.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/ti,tps65910.yaml
index f1a76f88fc0c..04f53568caa7 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/ti,tps65910.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/ti,tps65910.yaml
@@ -89,6 +89,14 @@ properties:
     type: boolean
     description: Keep high speed internal clock on in sleep state.
 
+  ti,keep-ext-sleep-control-on-shutdown:
+    type: boolean
+    description: |
+      Leave the external sleep control (EN1, EN2, SLEEP) of the regulators as
+      it is at shutdown. For boards on which removing it drops a rail that is
+      still in use, such as the CPU rail (EN1) of Tegra30 devices with
+      Windows RT firmware.
+
   regulators:
     type: object
     additionalProperties: false
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-asus-tf600t.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-asus-tf600t.dts
index 1ed0536ae3fa..5b445b219349 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-asus-tf600t.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-asus-tf600t.dts
@@ -1229,6 +1229,7 @@ pmic: pmic@2d {
 			ti,system-power-controller;
 			ti,sleep-keep-ck32k;
 			ti,sleep-enable;
+			ti,keep-ext-sleep-control-on-shutdown;
 
 			#gpio-cells = <2>;
 			gpio-controller;
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-lenovo-ideapad-yoga-11.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-lenovo-ideapad-yoga-11.dts
index 59af358c6be8..3ea144173ab2 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-lenovo-ideapad-yoga-11.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-lenovo-ideapad-yoga-11.dts
@@ -302,6 +302,7 @@ pmic: tps65911@2d {
 			interrupt-controller;
 
 			ti,system-power-controller;
+			ti,keep-ext-sleep-control-on-shutdown;
 
 			#gpio-cells = <2>;
 			gpio-controller;
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
index 3e1c579b07e1..a0f6b576f6f4 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
@@ -265,6 +265,7 @@ pmic: pmic@2d {
 			ti,system-power-controller;
 			ti,sleep-keep-ck32k;
 			ti,sleep-enable;
+			ti,keep-ext-sleep-control-on-shutdown;
 
 			#gpio-cells = <2>;
 			gpio-controller;
diff --git a/drivers/regulator/tps65910-regulator.c b/drivers/regulator/tps65910-regulator.c
index 3a3027e0b94e..c6c745581165 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/tps65910-regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/tps65910-regulator.c
@@ -314,6 +314,7 @@ struct tps65910_reg {
 	int  (*get_ctrl_reg)(int);
 	unsigned int *ext_sleep_control;
 	unsigned int board_ext_control[TPS65910_NUM_REGS];
+	bool keep_ext_control_on_shutdown;
 };
 
 static int tps65910_get_ctrl_register(int id)
@@ -1094,6 +1095,9 @@ static int tps65910_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	pmic->mfd = tps65910;
+	pmic->keep_ext_control_on_shutdown =
+		of_property_read_bool(tps65910->dev->of_node,
+				      "ti,keep-ext-sleep-control-on-shutdown");
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, pmic);
 
 	/* Give control of all register to control port */
@@ -1238,7 +1242,13 @@ static void tps65910_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 * value of the control signals are not in active state and before
 	 * bootloader initializes it, the system requires the rail output
 	 * to be active for booting.
+	 *
+	 * Boards on which removing the external control drops a rail that
+	 * is still in use opt out of this.
 	 */
+	if (pmic->keep_ext_control_on_shutdown)
+		return;
+
 	for (i = 0; i < pmic->num_regulators; i++) {
 		int err;
 		if (!pmic->rdev[i])
